  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Applied 50 EMA to GBPUSD 1H chart and observed price broke below it, confirming bearish bias and downtrend dominance.",
    "Step 2: Checked 4H chart to identify higher-time-frame structure, locating a strong demand zone at 1.25647 with multiple prior rejections as the long-term target.",
    "Step 3: Waited for and identified a bearish engulfing candlestick pattern at the 50 EMA on the 1H chart as the entry signal.",
    "Step 4: Opened two equal-sized short positions: first targeting 1:1 R:R, second targeting the 4H demand zone at 1.25647.",
    "Step 5: Monitored trade outcome: first position hit 1:1 target and was closed as a winner; second position remained open, with stop-loss kept above the swing high rather than moved to break-even."
  ],
  "outcome": "First position won at 1:1 R:R; second position still running at time of analysis.",
  "lessons": "Using multiple targets allows locking in partial profits early while letting the remainder run toward HTF confluence zones. Keeping the second stop above the swing high avoids premature exits during volatile approaches to key levels.",
